"{\"requirement\": \"Build a freestanding bookshelf with exactly four deep-red shelves. Each shelf should have a visibly curved front edge, and the top shelf must be smaller in width and depth than the three lower shelves. Add supporting side structure and place several distinct books or storage boxes on the shelves.\", \"articulation_required\": false, \"plan\": {\"object_name\": \"Freestanding four-shelf bookshelf with curved deep-red shelves\", \"components\": [{\"name\": \"shelf_1_bottom\", \"description\": \"Lowest of exactly four horizontal shelf slabs, centered near z=0.40. Deep-red finish; approximately 2.10 wide in x, 0.68 deep in y, and 0.10 thick in z. Construct the planform from a rectangular rear portion plus a shallow elliptical or cylindrical segment projecting toward the front (-y), producing a clearly visible smooth convex bowed front edge.\"}, {\"name\": \"shelf_2_lower_middle\", \"description\": \"Second horizontal shelf at approximately z=0.92, matching shelf_1 in width, depth, thickness, deep-red color, and convex curved front-edge construction.\"}, {\"name\": \"shelf_3_upper_middle\", \"description\": \"Third horizontal shelf at approximately z=1.44, matching the other two lower shelves in width, depth, thickness, deep-red color, and convex curved front-edge construction.\"}, {\"name\": \"shelf_4_top\", \"description\": \"Top and fourth shelf at approximately z=1.98. Centered over the lower shelves but visibly smaller in both width and depth: approximately 1.65 wide, 0.52 deep, and 0.10 thick. Use the same deep-red finish and convex bowed front edge facing -y.\"}, {\"name\": \"left_side_structure\", \"description\": \"Dark neutral or dark-wood freestanding support frame along the left side. Include a vertical rear upright near x=-1.12, a front leg near the front side, and short horizontal arms or brackets reaching inward to support the lower shelves. Extend from floor level to above the top shelf.\"}, {\"name\": \"right_side_structure\", \"description\": \"Mirror of the left support frame at x=+1.12, with matching upright, front leg, and shelf-supporting arms. Keep the two side structures visually balanced and structurally connected to all shelf levels.\"}, {\"name\": \"top_support_brackets\", \"description\": \"Pair of dark support brackets extending inward from the tall side uprights beneath the narrower top shelf. Their inner ends contact the underside of shelf_4_top so the reduced-width shelf does not appear to float.\"}, {\"name\": \"rear_cross_bracing\", \"description\": \"One or more narrow dark horizontal rear rails spanning between the left and right structures near the back (+y). Position rails beneath or behind shelf levels to stabilize the unit without forming an additional shelf.\"}, {\"name\": \"feet\", \"description\": \"Four compact floor-contact feet or leg ends beneath the side structures, arranged as left/right and front/back pairs. They hold the lowest shelf above the ground and make the bookshelf visibly freestanding.\"}, {\"name\": \"book_group_bottom\", \"description\": \"Several distinct upright books resting on shelf_1. Use separate narrow cuboids with varied heights, thicknesses, and colors; include one slightly tilted book if practical. Keep gaps between some volumes so they remain individually readable.\"}, {\"name\": \"storage_boxes_shelf_1\", \"description\": \"One or two storage boxes on the bottom shelf, modeled as box-like cuboids with contrasting colors and optional thinner lid pieces. Make their dimensions visibly different from the books.\"}, {\"name\": \"book_group_shelf_2\", \"description\": \"A second assortment of individually modeled books on shelf_2, with a different count, color sequence, and height profile from the bottom group. Include both upright books and a short horizontal stack.\"}, {\"name\": \"storage_box_shelf_3\", \"description\": \"A distinct medium storage box resting on shelf_3, offset to one side. Use a body and contrasting shallow lid or label panel so it is clearly identifiable as a container rather than another shelf.\"}, {\"name\": \"book_group_shelf_3\", \"description\": \"A small group of upright books beside the storage box on shelf_3. Vary their widths, heights, and colors, and keep all objects below the top shelf.\"}, {\"name\": \"top_shelf_objects\", \"description\": \"A sparse pair of small books or compact decorative storage boxes resting on shelf_4_top. Keep them centered enough to fit the reduced top-shelf depth and width.\"}], \"relations\": [\"Use world coordinates with +z upward, +x to the right, and the visible bookshelf front toward -y.\", \"The model contains exactly four components functioning as shelves: shelf_1_bottom, shelf_2_lower_middle, shelf_3_upper_middle, and shelf_4_top.\", \"All four shelves are horizontal, vertically ordered, and centered on x=0; their top surfaces are separated enough to hold books and boxes without intersection.\", \"The three lower shelves share approximately equal width and depth, while shelf_4_top is unambiguously narrower along x and shallower along y.\", \"Every shelf has a smooth convex front boundary projecting toward -y; the rear edge may remain straight near +y.\", \"The four shelf fronts should align generally around the same central x axis, while the smaller top shelf is set back or reduced in depth relative to the lower shelves.\", \"The left and right side structures are mirrored across the x=0 plane and stand outside the ends of the three lower shelves.\", \"Shelf ends contact or are closely supported by horizontal arms from the side structures; no shelf should appear suspended without support.\", \"The narrower top shelf is supported by inward-reaching top brackets connected to the taller outer side uprights.\", \"Rear cross-bracing connects the side structures near +y but remains narrow enough that it cannot be mistaken for a fifth shelf.\", \"All feet terminate at a common floor plane near z=0, and the overall center of mass reads as stable and freestanding.\", \"Books and storage boxes sit directly on shelf top surfaces with no visible gaps beneath them and no penetration into the shelf slabs.\", \"Shelf contents are distributed across multiple levels and remain distinct through variations in dimensions, placement, orientation, and color.\", \"Objects placed near the curved fronts remain behind the forward-most bowed edge and do not overhang excessively.\", \"Deep red is reserved prominently for all four shelf slabs; supports should use a contrasting dark wood, charcoal, or near-black appearance so the shelf count and curved geometry remain legible.\"], \"critic_checklist\": [\"Verify there are exactly four horizontal deep-red shelf slabs and no fifth shelf-like platform.\", \"Verify all four shelf front edges are visibly curved in top or perspective view, not merely straight cuboid fronts.\", \"Verify the curved side faces inherit the shelf color and remain smooth enough to read as a continuous bow.\", \"Verify the top shelf is measurably smaller than each lower shelf in both x width and y depth.\", \"Verify the three lower shelves have consistent overall width and depth.\", \"Verify all shelves are centered and ordered from bottom to top without overlap.\", \"Verify left and right supporting structures are present, mirrored, floor-reaching, and visibly connected to the shelving system.\", \"Verify the narrow top shelf has explicit support brackets or arms and does not float between distant uprights.\", \"Verify rear rails or braces are too narrow to be interpreted as additional shelves.\", \"Verify the unit contacts the floor through stable feet or legs and does not rely on a wall for support.\", \"Verify several distinct books or storage boxes are present on multiple shelves, with recognizable differences in size, color, or orientation.\", \"Verify every book and box rests on a shelf top and does not intersect adjacent shelves, supports, or other contents.\", \"Verify shelf contents do not conceal 